<section class="p-hero"><div class="p-hero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/farm-barn.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/farm-barn-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/farm-barn.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.15"></div><div class="wrap p-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/where-we-work/">Where we work</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Lancaster</span></nav><p class="kicker">South Central PA</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Lancaster, PA</h1><p class="lede">From the brick rows of downtown Lancaster to stone farmhouses and bank barns out in the townships, this county&#x27;s buildings are old, solid and expensive to repair the right way.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line-light" href="/contact-us/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Lancaster County</dd></div><div><dt>Housing</dt><dd>Brick rows, stone farmhouses &amp; barns</dd></div><div><dt>Storm on record</dt><dd>Valentine&#x27;s Day ice storm, 2007</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="peril-box"><p class="peril-h">Common local claim risks</p><ul class="chips"><li>Hail</li><li>Wind &amp; thunderstorms</li><li>Barn &amp; outbuilding damage</li><li>Sinkholes</li><li>Lightning &amp; fire</li></ul></div>

<h2>The buildings that define the county</h2>
<p>Lancaster County's landscape is full of buildings that standard estimating software doesn't handle well. In the city, Cabbage Hill, the downtown core and the neighborhoods around Franklin &amp; Marshall have brick rowhomes and townhouses, many with slate roofs, cornices and tall plaster walls. Out in the townships, around Lititz, Ephrata, Strasburg, Leola and Elizabethtown, stone farmhouses stand beside bank barns built into the hillside, with heavy timber frames and stone foundations.</p>
<p>Repairing these structures properly means stonemasons who work in lime mortar, framers who can replace a damaged timber, and roofers who still install slate. When a carrier's estimate swaps those trades for generic line items, the gap can be large.</p>
<h2>Farms, barns and outbuildings</h2>
<p>Lancaster County is one of the most productive farm counties in the country, and its farms include dairy, poultry, produce and more. Barns, silos, poultry houses and machine sheds are exposed to wind, hail, heavy snow and lightning. Common disputes include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Barn roof and siding damage valued at depreciated cost with little explanation.</li>
<li>Whether a damaged timber frame can be repaired or must be rebuilt.</li>
<li>Equipment and stored crops or feed lost in an outbuilding fire.</li>
<li>Code and permit requirements when an agricultural building is replaced.</li>
</ul>
<p>Farm policies vary widely, and many have their own limits for outbuildings and contents. Our <a href="/property-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-claim-appraisal/">commercial claim appraisal</a> service covers farm and business losses as well as residential ones.</p>
<h3>A note on Plain communities</h3>
<p>Lancaster County is home to a large Amish and Old Order Mennonite population. Some Plain families take part in church-based aid plans rather than buying commercial insurance, while others, along with many neighboring farms and businesses, carry conventional policies. Our work is limited to claims under insurance policies, and we approach every property owner with the same respect for their time, their buildings and their way of doing things.</p>
<h2>Hail, wind and ice</h2>
<p>South-central Pennsylvania sees more hail than the eastern part of the state, and summer thunderstorms can drop hail and straight-line winds across a wide swath of farmland and subdivisions. The Valentine's Day ice storm of 2007 coated the region in ice and brought down trees and limbs. Hail claims often turn into arguments over whether damage is functional or cosmetic, and whether new shingles can match the old. Our <a href="/property-appraisal-services/roof-hail-damage-appraisal/">roof and hail damage appraisal</a> service tackles those disputes directly.</p>
<h2>Limestone and sinkholes</h2>
<p>Much of Lancaster County sits on limestone, and sinkholes are a known hazard in parts of the county. Many policies exclude or limit earth movement and sinkhole damage, so the policy wording is critical. If coverage is denied, talk to a Pennsylvania attorney. If coverage is accepted but the amount is disputed, appraisal can help.</p>
<h2>Along the Susquehanna</h2>
<p>River towns like Columbia and Marietta lie along the Susquehanna, and Agnes in 1972 flooded parts of the county. Rising water is excluded from homeowner policies and handled through a flood policy such as NFIP, with its own process; homeowner appraisal doesn't reach it.</p>

<h2>Services available in Lancaster</h2>
<p>Every Pennsylvania Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in Lancaster and the rest of Lancaster County, including:</p>
<ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/property-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisal-services/home-insurance-claim-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-claim-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisal-services/roof-hail-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisal-services/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Wind &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisal-services/tropical-storm-remnant-appraisal/">Tropical Storm Remnant Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisal-services/water-damage-claim-appraisal/">Water Damage Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisal-services/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Lancaster property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can appraisal be used for a barn or outbuilding claim?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, if your farm or homeowner policy has an appraisal clause and the disagreement is about the amount of loss. Outbuildings often have separate limits, so it&#x27;s worth reading those first.</p></div></details><details><summary>Why is stone farmhouse repair so expensive?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Historic stone walls usually need lime-based mortar and experienced masons. Using modern mortar can damage old stone, so the proper method costs more, and a fair estimate should reflect it.</p></div></details></div>
